$ /mnt/ssd/proyectos/SLDB_1/IR/.venv/bin/specir about
specir — semantic specs -> diagrams -> catalog HTML (specIR's visual layer over sldb)

Where the diagrams live:
  spec files       : YAML specs (`type:` one of the eight diagram types) next to their vistas.yml
  store            : /mnt/ssd/proyectos/SLDB_1/deskops/.sldb
  specs in a store : SpecDoc documents (`sldb notations list --store <.sldb>`)
  catalog config   : a vistas.yml registry or a project.yml / diagram-store config

Flow to HTML:
  1. specir diagram validate <spec.yml>
  2. specir diagram render   <spec.yml> --out <dir>
  3. specir diagram lint     <rendered.mmd>
  4. specir catalog build    --config <vistas.yml> --out <out.html>
     (build alias = catalog build; --atoms-dir injects window.ATOMS_DB)

Into the store (sldb, used directly):
  sldb notations sync --spec <spec.yml> --store <.sldb>
  sldb notations sync --catalog <vistas.yml> [--check] --store <.sldb>
  sldb notations from-graph --python <src_dir> | --store <.sldb> | --snapshot <graph.json>
  sldb notations view <SpecDoc id> --store <.sldb>

Save a built catalog's annotations (replaces spec2viz's `catalog serve`):
  sldb models add specir.visual.catalog.annotations:CatalogAnnotationsDoc --store <.sldb>
  sldb serve --store <.sldb> --cors --port 8765
  specir catalog build --config <vistas.yml> --out <out.html> --sldb-url http://127.0.0.1:8765
